---
import InsertLayout from '../../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/jsonld';
import { KIT_VERSION } from '../../config/kit';
import licenceText from '../../data/kit-license.txt?raw';
import '../../styles/kit.css';

const jsonLd = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Migration Acceptance Kit', url: '/kit/' },
  { name: 'Licence', url: '/kit/license/' }
]);
---

<InsertLayout
  title="Migration Acceptance Kit licence"
  description="The full commercial licence for the Toledo Migration Acceptance Kit, published before purchase: what the buyer may do, what they may not, the refund policy, the warranty and the liability limit."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  heading="Migration Acceptance Kit licence"
  subheading="Published in full, before purchase, so nobody has to ask for it."
>
  <p class="kit-kicker">
    Licence version 1.0 &middot; kit release {KIT_VERSION}
  </p>

  <p>
    This is the licence a buyer of the
    <a href="/kit/">Migration Acceptance Kit</a> receives. It is a commercial licence:
    not MIT, not Apache, not open source. It is published here in full so your legal
    team can read it without contacting anyone and without creating an account.
  </p>
  <p>
    The short version, which the text below says at greater length: you may run
    it, read all the source, change it, copy it anywhere inside your
    organisation and keep it forever; you may not redistribute or resell the kit
    itself. The reports it produces are yours outright with no strings. Refunds
    are 30 days, no reason required.
  </p>
  <p class="kit-note">
    Section 10 says plainly that this was drafted by Toledo in plain English and
    has not been reviewed by an attorney. If your counsel needs different
    wording, a clause struck, or an entity name on an order form, email
    <a href="mailto:dev@toledotechnologies.com">dev@toledotechnologies.com</a>.
    Reasonable requests are normal and are not a problem.
  </p>

  <h2>Full text</h2>
  <div class="kit-licence-text">{licenceText}</div>

  <div class="kit-links">
    <a href="/kit/">Back to the kit &rarr;</a>
    <a href="/kit/acceptance-checklist/"
      >Read the acceptance checklist (free) &rarr;</a
    >
    <a href="/terms">Site terms &rarr;</a>
  </div>
</InsertLayout>
